#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Daily creative build for the Jeb mod (approved by the user 2026-10-23,
hardened 2026-10-23).

Copies the mod (../mod, beside this script) to a staging folder and lets a headless
Sonnet session build one new thing there (it reads brief.md beside this script). It has no
web access and no subagents; its Bash runs in a sandbox that can read only the
staging folder and the tools it needs, write only there, and reach no network.
After it exits, the runner copies staging to a folder of its own and gates that
copy. Only a build that passes every gate is synced into the mod, in place; the
old mod is backed up first. A failed build is thrown away.

  jeb-creative-build             build, gate, swap in on success
  jeb-creative-build --task TEXT build as above, with a one-off request from the owner added to the
                                 builder's prompt (up to 1000 printable characters; the run record
                                 notes only that one was given, with its length and a short hash)
  jeb-creative-build --dry-run   copy and gate the current mod, no model run
  jeb-creative-build --rollback  restore the most recent backup
  jeb-creative-build --status    last runs and backups

Gates: no links, special files or unexpected dot names in staging; only the
allowed file kinds; pinned files unchanged; every existing test kept verbatim and
still passing; no new hooks, engine calls or env access (from `claude plugin
validate --json`, plus the regex audits); size limits; plugin validate, the
pinned tsc and the test suite twice with 0 failures; a non-empty change. The
news file is then written into the gate copy and the whole gate runs again.
"""

